            <ArticleTitle>Angioplasty catheter communication mimicking coronary arterial dissection.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>401-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case in which a sudden communication between the pressure and balloon inflation lumens of a percutaneous transluminal angioplasty (PTCA) catheter angiographically mimicked dissection of the coronary artery. This case illustrates a previously undescribed catheter artifact that must be differentiated from other complications of PTCA.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
